    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="fc24f6cf-b3ad-5f06-9257-b092e20f522c" activityNameId="8a902f84-cdf3-5f20-8af0-0d8aaf681ae9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production MX, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production MX, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 100% of the imported Mexican natural gas to US was imported by pipeline and 0% as LNG. An average distance of 700 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Mexico, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are  km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=5c5ccca5-13e2-3f06-a78d-94fb8548a941
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Mexican natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5c5ccca5-13e2-3f06-a78d-94fb8548a941.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
